    "troubleshooting": [
      {
        "symptom": "The dish tastes bland and the sauce feels dry",
        "likely_cause": "Underseasoned tomatoes, under-ripe tomatoes, or low-quality olive oil",
        "prevention": "Use peak-season summer tomatoes, generously salt the tomatoes during the marination phase, and use the best quality extra virgin olive oil available.",
        "fix": "Add an extra pinch of flaky sea salt, a splash of high-quality olive oil, and a tiny squeeze of fresh lemon juice to brighten the flavors right before serving."
      }
    ],
    "chef_notes": [
      "The success of this dish entirely depends on the quality of your ingredients. Use the ripest, sweetest cherry tomatoes you can find.",
      "Tossing hot pasta with the raw tomato mixture slightly warms the sauce and helps the starch from the pasta bind with the tomato juices and olive oil to create a light emulsion.",
      "Do not refrigerate the tomatoes before using them; cold temperatures dull their flavor and alter their texture.",
      "To easily customize this dish, consider adding fresh mozzarella pearls, toasted pine nuts, capers, or a splash of balsamic glaze."
    ],
    "cultural_context": "Often referred to as Pasta alla Checca in Rome, this style of raw tomato and herb sauce is an Italian summer staple. It was born out of the necessity to utilize abundant summer garden yields without heating up the kitchen for extended periods.",
